#import "../helpers/shared.typ": req, budget, src, supply, pitfall
= Broader Impacts <sec-broader-impacts>
#budget(0.4, 240)

#req(source: "PAPPG — VERIFY BEFORE SUBMISSION")[
The Project Description must contain a separate section labeled "Broader Impacts."
*Asserted by the bot from general PAPPG structure, not a direct read of Ch. II.D.2.d.
Confirm in the PAPPG PDF. A missing required labeled section is a compliance failure.*
]

#src("SOL", "§II — Measures of Success")[
"Proposals should advance one or more of the following measures of success."
*Discovery and Innovation*: data sets established or expanded; start-ups created; new
technologies or techniques established. *STEM Education and Workforce*: participants hired
into a STEM related field. *Research Infrastructure*: new infrastructure built.
]

#src("W1", "video_summary")[
NSF stresses measuring the *impact* of open-source ecosystems — discovery, innovation,
STEM education — "rather than just their health." Contributor counts and download figures
are health metrics; they are not by themselves impact.
]

#src("W2", "video_summary — Government-Focused Projects")[
Narrowness warning: a project whose only target audience is government "might be seen as
too narrow." Demonstrate a broader audience.
]

#supply[
- Selected measures of success from NSF's enumerated list, with per-measure evidence
- Impact claims distinguished from health metrics
- Educational/workforce dimension: current and planned adoption, student contributors
- Breadth of audience beyond any single sector
]
